shadowfetch-defaults (2.0.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * 2.0.1 — installer and discoverability fixes found by reading public
    reviews.
  * Ship AGENTS.md uncompressed (override_dh_compress -XAGENTS.md).
    dh_compress gzipped it, so shadowfetch-agent-guide.desktop execed a
    path that did not exist and the AI Agent Setup Guide menu entry did
    nothing at all.
  * shadowfetch-llm.desktop: drop ConsoleOnly from Categories. Per the
    XDG spec it hides an entry from graphical menus, so Pick a Local AI
    Model never appeared in the KDE menu.
  * Group the seven on-device AI applications under a new Local AI menu
    category; they were scattered across Utility, System, Network and
    Development with nothing tying them together.
  * Print the Shadowfetch brand mark in shadowfetch-hermes and
    shadowfetch-agents (ANSI, no new dependency).

